    "amount_sgd": 3.20,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.20,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the SGD 4.00 no-show fee stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.20 of it (80 percent), the platform retaining the residual SGD 0.80. I ran the four POL-NS-01 conditions on the trip record, the GPS trace, the chat log and the fare ledger. Arrival: the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 21:58:18, and the GPS trace's first in-geofence fix falls at the same second, 0.11 m from the pickup pin and well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, with 46 consecutive qualifying fixes - limbs (a) and (b) hold. Dwell: one continuous in-geofence run of 454 seconds, 21:58:18 to 22:05:52, against the 300 second free waiting period in trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec - a surplus, not a shortfall. Limb (d): the trip was terminated by the driver at 22:05:55 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the dwell elapsed, with no boarding event. The rider's arguments do not change this. His submission that the driver had not located him, drawn from the driver's 21:58:48 message ('I am at the bay, which door are you at'), is rejected: limb (d)'s own test is the recorded cancellation reason code, and the code recorded is RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three limb (d) recognises; DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE is not on the record, and the record contradicts it. The rider's own device places him stationary (0.0 km/h in all 72 fixes) between 606 m and 613 m from the pin across the whole window - he was not walking to the bay, and he neither sent a message nor replied to the driver's. POL-NS-04 therefore cannot exonerate him (limb (a) fails for want of any rider message; limb (c) fails on his own track), and POL-NS-11 does not arise because the rider track is present. POL-NS-03 wrong-entrance does not apply: the driver's stationary fixes lie inside the arrival radius, not outside it, and the trip carries 1 registered pickup point, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises. POL-NS-05 does not apply: at the arrival timestamp the driver was 0.11 m from the pin and stationary, so the BUTTON marker is not false and no waiting-clock recomputation is needed. POL-NS-06 gives nothing: the 454 s dwell exceeds the 300 s minimum, so the MISSING traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02704-01, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT - disclosed, and relied on only for its absence) cannot matter, and no interval-summing is required. The rider's POL-NS-10 submissions are correct and afford him nothing (the trip was terminated by the driver, was not scheduled, and the fare ledger's waiting-time line is SGD 0.00). Compensation is fixed by POL-NS-07 at 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee, SGD 3.20, matching the driver_compensation figure the fare ledger computes, and the anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below 4, and 2 of 111 completed trips is 0.018, below 0.08. Confidence is 0.9, above the 0.70 floor. The cap is 1.0: the deciding facts are carried by artifacts at weight_multiplier 1.0 (trip record, GPS trace, fare ledger, driver profile), and nothing carrying a deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08 - no clock skew, a 0.0 s maximum trace gap at 100 percent coverage, the chat log matches trip_record.chat_message_count, and the SGD 4.00 cancellation-fee line reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires, so the case does not escalate. No clause produces a referral: there is no false-arrival record under POL-NS-05(ii), no mis-selected-code driver-education item under POL-NS-01 because limb (d) is satisfied on the code actually recorded, and no POL-NS-07 escalation packet because the anti-farming check does not trip. Per POL-GEN-03, on a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd, so SGD 3.20 in both fields; the rider's own charge is untouched. Under POL-GEN-05 the monetary effect, SGD 3.20, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold and executes automatically. This is an automated, provisional ruling; either party may appeal once under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

